Host-side project tests (no hardware required, run from the project root):

- node test/decoder.test.js
    Decoder regression tests for chirpstack/decoder.js: CayenneLPP metric and
    imperial (rain/pressure resolution), debug channels (Generic Sensor and
    legacy Analog Input), binary version 1 (older firmware) and unknown
    versions.

- node test/payload_roundtrip.test.js
    Compiles src/payload_binary.cpp together with test/payload_roundtrip.cpp
    for the host (c++/g++/clang++, CXX overrides; skipped if none is found),
    encodes known measurement sets (metric, imperial, minimal, out of range,
    PCB v2.0 I/O block incl. VE.Direct)
    and checks that decoder.js returns the same values - and clamps instead
    of wrapping.

- node test/vedirect.test.js
    Compiles src/vedirect.cpp with test/vedirect_parser.cpp for the host and
    feeds it Victron VE.Direct text-protocol streams: MPPT and BMV blocks,
    corrupt checksums, interleaved HEX messages, a mid-stream start and
    "---" values.

- node test/firmware_runtime.test.js
    Compiles the real sensors, board I/O, parameter, JSON and LoRa transport
    modules with deterministic hardware fakes. Exercises stuck/recovered
    1-Wire conversions, output/PWM shutdown, battery hysteresis and missing
    VE.Direct/PV data, standalone wind 2, energy-setting save/read-back,
    bounded radio/join retries, node cleanup, timer rollover and JSON >1024
    bytes. Requires a C++11 compiler and the ArduinoJson dependency restored
    by the normal PlatformIO build. Does not flash or simulate physical timing.

Run all scripts together: node --test test/*.test.js

These are plain Node.js scripts, not PlatformIO unit tests; `pio test` is
not used in this project.
